  "notes": "### Fixed\n- Mac Calendar no longer turns itself off after an update. Pyxida is now signed with a stable identity, so macOS keeps your Calendar permission across updates. After installing this version, macOS may ask for Calendar access one last time.\n- The New menu shortcuts work with Greek and other keyboard layouts.\n\n### Added\n- Change your Sync passphrase, also right after unlocking with your recovery key.\n- Each Sync passphrase screen explains what the passphrase is, with a quick way to use your recovery key.\n- Terminal theme: green on black, like an old console.\n\n### Changed\n- Settings shows Appearance once, with the theme swatches as the only control.\n- Your recovery key is saved outside the Pyxida folder, and Sync warns if it finds one inside.",
